msgid "Show the Create Child Theme tool in the menu."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the plugin name (its wp-admin menu).
#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/child-theme-tool.js:23
#, js-format
msgid "Shows the Create Child Theme screen in the %s menu. It’s usually a one-time tool — turn this on when you need to generate a child theme, and off again after to tidy the menu and unregister the tool’s theme-writing endpoints. Turning it off never touches a child theme you’ve already generated."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/forms.js:16
msgid "Build forms from blocks — fields, submit, messages."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/forms.js:20
msgid "Adds a Form block suite to the editor: text, email, phone, URL, number, date, hidden, and consent fields, dropdowns, radio and checkbox groups, a submit button, and success and error messages authored as blocks. Forms live in your content — drop one in as a pattern, restyle it with the theme, no shortcodes. Submissions are validated on the server, emailed to you, and kept in a Forms inbox (with a per-form auto-responder) even when email delivery fails."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/popups.js:16
msgid "Design popups and slide-ins in the block editor."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/popups.js:20
msgid "Adds a Popups screen where each popup is a normal block-editor document — design it with any blocks, then set its position (a centered modal or a corner slide-in), trigger (time on page, scroll depth, exit intent, or a manual link), display rules, and how often returning visitors see it. Popups keep firing even if the plugin is later deactivated."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/scripts.js:16
msgid "Show the Scripts editor in the menu."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/scripts.js:17
msgid "Shows the Scripts screen for adding header, body, and footer code — analytics, pixels, and the like. Turning it off only hides the editor; your scripts keep printing on the front end. Use the master switch inside the Scripts screen to actually stop output."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/seo.js:15
msgid "Basic SEO"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/seo.js:16
msgid "Search titles, descriptions, schema, and a live preview."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/seo.js:20
msgid "Adds an SEO panel to the page and post editor: a custom search title, a meta description, a schema type (Article or FAQ), a hide-from-search-engines switch, and a live preview of the search result. The front end emits the matching title tag, meta description, Open Graph tags for social sharing, and schema.org structured data. If a dedicated SEO plugin (Yoast, Rank Math, AIOSEO, SEOPress…) is active, Blocklane’s output stands down automatically so tags are never doubled."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/site-privacy.js:16
msgid "Show the Site Visibility controls in the menu."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/advanced/rows/site-privacy.js:17
msgid "Shows the Site Visibility screen — a password or maintenance page for visitors, plus search-engine indexing. Turning it off only hides the screen; whatever visibility you’ve set stays in effect. While a lock is active the screen stays visible no matter this toggle, so a private site can never be stranded with no way to unlock it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:105
msgid "Duplicate Content"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:106
msgid "Clone posts, pages, and custom post types."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:107
msgid "Adds a “Clone” link to the row actions on Posts, Pages, and custom post types. Cloning copies the content, custom fields, and taxonomy terms into a new draft, ready to edit."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:114
msgid "Reorder Content"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:115
msgid "Drag to set a manual order — and group pages."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:119
msgid "Adds a “Sort by Order” view where you can drag rows into a manual order, and orders the chosen post types by that on the front end. Queries that ask for a specific order — like recent posts or events — still win, so use it for content like team members, testimonials, or services. Pages (and other nestable types) also become a collapsible tree: a chevron on any parent page hides or shows everything nested under it, and Indent/Outdent row actions move pages into or out of a group — the same parent/child structure as the page editor’s Parent setting, just faster to arrange. With this on, the Pages screen shows the whole tree on one page; very large sites (500+ pages) stay paginated instead, and “Sort by Order” opens the full tree on demand."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:126
msgid "Replace Media"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:127
msgid "Swap a file in place, keeping the same URL."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:128
msgid "Adds a “Replace file” action in the media library, next to Download. Upload a new file of the same type and it swaps in place — same URL and filename — so every post and reference keeps working. Thumbnails regenerate automatically."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:135
msgid "Disable Comments"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:136
msgid "Turn off the entire comment system site-wide."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:140
msgid "Switches comments off everywhere: closes comments and pings on all content, hides the comment blocks and feeds on the front end, removes the Comments admin menu, metaboxes, dashboard widget, and toolbar item, and limits the comment REST endpoints to editor notes to cut spam and enumeration. Editor notes (WordPress 7.1) keep working — they are an editorial tool for logged-in editors, not public comments. Nothing is deleted — existing comments are just hidden and come back if you turn this off. Leave it off for blogs or news sites that need discussion."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:147
msgid "Disable Blog Features"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:148
msgid "Strip rarely-used blogging features for non-blogs."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:152
msgid "Cleans up blogging leftovers most sites never use. Disables Post Formats (drops post-format theme support — hiding the editor’s format panel where a theme offers one — and removes the Default Post Format setting), and on Settings → Writing hides Post via Email and stops the default Update Services (ping-o-matic) pings sent when you publish. Your default category stays. Nothing is deleted and it all reverts when turned off — leave it off for blogs or news sites."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:161
msgid "Auto-Update Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:162
msgid "Install plugin updates automatically as they ship."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:166
msgid "Outdated plugins are the #1 way WordPress sites get compromised, so this is the single highest-impact setting here. While on, it applies to all plugins and overrides their individual auto-update settings."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:174
msgid "Auto-Update Themes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:175
msgid "Install theme updates automatically as they ship."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:179
msgid "Keeps every installed theme current. While on, it applies to all themes and overrides their individual settings. (Core minor releases already auto-update by default.)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:186
msgid "Limit Post Revisions"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:187
msgid "Cap stored revisions to keep the DB lean."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:188
msgid "Caps how many revisions WordPress keeps per post so the database doesn’t grow without bound. Set the number below; use 0 to turn revisions off entirely."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:195
msgid "Limit the WordPress Heartbeat"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:196
msgid "Slow the admin polling that hits admin-ajax."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:200
msgid "The WordPress Heartbeat polls admin-ajax.php every 15–60 seconds to power autosave and post-locking — steady background load, especially on shared hosting. This throttles it to the interval below and turns it off entirely on the front end (public pages don’t need it). Autosave and post-locking keep working, just less often. Set the interval below."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:209
msgid "Limit Login Attempts"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:210
msgid "Slow down brute-force attacks on the login form."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:214
msgid "Locks out an IP address for a few minutes after 5 failed logins, blunting password brute-forcing on wp-login. Behind a reverse proxy or CDN this keys on the proxy address; some hosts already rate-limit logins at the edge."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:222
msgid "Disable XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:223
msgid "Turn off /xmlrpc.php to close a common attack surface."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:227
msgid "Closes brute-force amplification and pingback abuse. Leave this off if you use the WordPress mobile app, Jetpack, or remote publishing, which rely on XML-RPC. Some managed hosts already block it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:235
msgid "Disable Theme & Plugin File Editing"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:236
msgid "Remove the dashboard code editors."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:237
msgid "Defines DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT so a compromised admin account can’t run PHP through the built-in Appearance and Plugins code editors. No effect on normal editing. Some managed hosts set this already."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:245
msgid "Block User Enumeration"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:246
msgid "Stop bots from harvesting your usernames."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:247
msgid "Redirects ?author= probes and removes the public REST user list, so bots can’t collect your usernames to target brute-force attacks. Doesn’t affect logged-in editing or the block editor. Usually not covered by hosts."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:254
msgid "Safe SVG Uploads"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:255
msgid "Upload SVGs — sanitized automatically."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:256
msgid "Allows SVG uploads in the media library and sanitizes every file on the way in, stripping scripts and other unsafe markup. Anything that can’t be cleaned is rejected, so a malicious SVG can’t carry code into your library."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:263
msgid "Last Login Column"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:264
msgid "See when each user last signed in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:265
msgid "Adds a “Last Login” column to the Users screen, showing when each account last signed in (and how long ago), so you can spot dormant or shared accounts."
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:272
msgid "Clean Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:273
msgid "Delete removes every remaining Blocklane setting too."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the plugin name.
#: inc/onboarding/src/screens/AdvancedScreen.js:280
#, js-format
msgid "Deleting %s always stops what it renders — forms, popups, menus, content types, dynamic values — because everything runs from the plugin itself. By default it leaves two things behind, because they are yours rather than plugin state: your uploaded SVG icons and your Custom Scripts code. A reinstall picks both back up. Turn this on and Delete clears those as well, along with every remaining Blocklane setting. Your content records — pages, entries, terms, form submissions — are kept either way. Leave this off unless you are removing Blocklane for good."
msgstr ""

